/**
 * @file aes
 * @author jung-kwang lee (ntoskrnl7@gmail.com)
 * @brief AES block cipher (FIPS 197)
 *
 * Follows the NIST FIPS 197 specification. Neither the S-box nor the round
 * transformation tables are written out in the source; they are generated at
 * compile time from the algebraic definition given in the specification, that
 * is the multiplicative inverse in GF(2^8) followed by an affine
 * transformation. Since no table is transcribed, a transcription error is not
 * possible, and a few values stated in the specification are checked with
 * static_assert so that a faulty generation is caught at compile time.
 *
 * @version 0.1
 *
 * @copyright Copyright (c) 2022 C++ Cryptographics template library Authors
 *
 */
